From 8604b185b77b13d0c53f92853e9bb94ce8a001b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pauli Virtanen <pav@iki.fi>
Date: Sun, 29 Mar 2026 16:43:01 +0300
Subject: Bluetooth: hci_conn: fix potential UAF in set_cig_params_sync
Patch-mainline: v7.0-rc7
Git-commit: a2639a7f0f5bf7d73f337f8f077c19415c62ed2c
References: CVE-2026-43019 bsc#1264003

hci_conn lookup and field access must be covered by hdev lock in
set_cig_params_sync, otherwise it's possible it is freed concurrently.

Take hdev lock to prevent hci_conn from being deleted or modified
concurrently.  Just RCU lock is not suitable here, as we also want to
avoid "tearing" in the configuration.

Fixes: a091289218202 ("Bluetooth: hci_conn: Fix hci_le_set_cig_params")
Signed-off-by: Pauli Virtanen <pav@iki.fi>
Signed-off-by: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
[ backport: adjusted lock/unlock calls to stack-allocated pdu ]
Assisted-by: Gemini:gemini-1.5-pro
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>
---
 net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c
index 5edab2769f2b..89a16da04648 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c
@@ -1743,9 +1743,13 @@ static int set_cig_params_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev, void *data)
 	struct iso_cig_params pdu;
 	u8 cis_id;
 
+	hci_dev_lock(hdev);
+
 	conn = hci_conn_hash_lookup_cig(hdev, cig_id);
-	if (!conn)
+	if (!conn) {
+		hci_dev_unlock(hdev);
 		return 0;
+	}
 
 	memset(&pdu, 0, sizeof(pdu));
 
@@ -1785,6 +1789,8 @@ static int set_cig_params_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev, void *data)
 		cis->p_rtn  = qos->ucast.in.rtn;
 	}
 
+	hci_dev_unlock(hdev);
+
 	if (!pdu.cp.num_cis)
 		return 0;
 
-- 
